  "notes": "West leads the ♦K against 4♠. West wins the opening diamond lead and continues the suit. If South ruffs in dummy, he may soon be in trouble. West is marked with the ♠A and ♣K for his 1NT opening. The contract will no longer be makable if West started with 3 spades and 2 hearts.\n\nIf South unblocks the ♥A and plays a spade, West will win the ♠A and continue the suit. South will be unable to get all of his club losers away on the hearts before West ruffs. West will still have an exit card in diamonds and South will be left with a loser in clubs.\n\nSouth can guard against this distribution by discarding a club from dummy at trick 2. West will continue a small trump, won in dummy. When East follows, the contract is certain.\n\nSouth should unblock the ♥A and play a second round of trumps. West will win the ♠A, but he will be powerless to stop South from getting 3 discards on dummy's hearts. If West returns a diamond, South must take the ruff in the closed hand.\n\nNorth's remaining spade honour will take care of West's last trump. The lead will be in dummy so that South can enjoy the hearts.",
  "commentary_paragraphs": [
    "West leads the ♦K against 4♠. West wins the opening diamond lead and continues the suit. If South ruffs in dummy, he may soon be in trouble. West is marked with the ♠A and ♣K for his 1NT opening. The contract will no longer be makable if West started with 3 spades and 2 hearts.",
    "If South unblocks the ♥A and plays a spade, West will win the ♠A and continue the suit. South will be unable to get all of his club losers away on the hearts before West ruffs. West will still have an exit card in diamonds and South will be left with a loser in clubs.",
    "South can guard against this distribution by discarding a club from dummy at trick 2. West will continue a small trump, won in dummy. When East follows, the contract is certain.",
    "South should unblock the ♥A and play a second round of trumps. West will win the ♠A, but he will be powerless to stop South from getting 3 discards on dummy's hearts. If West returns a diamond, South must take the ruff in the closed hand.",
    "North's remaining spade honour will take care of West's last trump. The lead will be in dummy so that South can enjoy the hearts."
  ],
